1
00:00:05,956 --> 00:00:06,844
A Real Stewart

2
00:00:06,844 --> 00:00:12,027
There's nothing more joyous than the arrival of a new baby.

3
00:00:12,027 --> 00:00:13,037
I am so excited. Mother!

4
00:00:13,037 --> 00:00:16,390
Just imagine--Marilyn and Richard must be thrilled!

5
00:00:16,390 --> 00:00:21,333
Oh, a new baby!

6
00:00:21,333 --> 00:00:22,793
Max ... Max ... Max.

7
00:00:22,793 --> 00:00:30,186
Oh, it's a sweet-sounding name for a sweet little boy.

8
00:00:30,186 --> 00:00:31,403
My first grandchild.

9
00:00:31,403 --> 00:00:33,358
And my first nephew.

10
00:00:33,358 --> 00:00:35,736
Isn't he just adorable?

11
00:00:35,736 --> 00:00:38,714
He looks a lot like you, Mom. He does.

12
00:00:38,714 --> 00:00:41,692
Do you think so?

13
00:00:41,692 --> 00:00:46,284
Well, I guess. He does look a lot like Richard,

14
00:00:46,284 --> 00:00:48,847
and I guess he looks a lot like me.

15
00:00:48,847 --> 00:00:51,059
Oh, he's got Richard's eyes, though.

16
00:00:51,059 --> 00:00:55,103
I really want Harry and Michelle to see Max.

17
00:00:55,103 --> 00:00:57,581
When are they coming?

18
00:00:57,581 --> 00:01:00,793
Tomorrow. Harry has an account to work on today.

19
00:01:00,793 --> 00:01:04,337
Yes, he does have Richard's eyes. Big blue eyes.

20
00:01:04,337 --> 00:01:07,955
[01:20.17]The baby even looks at you like Richard does.

21
00:01:07,955 --> 00:01:11,293
Well, children usually resemble their parents.

22
00:01:11,293 --> 00:01:12,013
It's true.

23
00:01:12,013 --> 00:01:15,116
Michelle is a lot like Harry in so many ways.

24
00:01:15,116 --> 00:01:20,405
And she's shy with new people, just like he is.

25
00:01:20,405 --> 00:01:22,119
You really like Michelle, don't you?

26
00:01:22,119 --> 00:01:25,233
Yes. I'm very fond of her.

27
00:01:25,233 --> 00:01:26,361
And Harry, too?

28
00:01:26,361 --> 00:01:29,339
Well ...

29
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:34,117
Uh, it's four-thirty. Oh my!

30
00:01:34,117 --> 00:01:37,651
Marilyn and Richard will be home from the hospital any minute,

31
00:01:37,651 --> 00:01:39,597
and we must prepare this room.

32
00:01:39,597 --> 00:01:42,645
Where will we put all the presents?

33
00:01:42,645 --> 00:01:45,202
Well, let's take everything to the living room.

34
00:01:45,202 --> 00:01:50,183
Marilyn and Richard and the baby need the space.

35
00:01:50,183 --> 00:01:53,163
It's crowded in here.

36
00:01:53,163 --> 00:01:56,140
The welcome sign is up:

37
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:57,160
"Welcome home, Max."

38
00:01:57,160 --> 00:01:59,118
Isn't it exciting, Grandpa?

39
00:01:59,118 --> 00:02:03,096
Your first great-grandchild.

40
00:02:03,096 --> 00:02:06,407
Yes. Yes, sir.

41
00:02:06,407 --> 00:02:09,039
A great-grandchild. A great-grandson.

42
00:02:09,039 --> 00:02:13,030
Another generation to carry on the Stewart name.

43
00:02:13,030 --> 00:02:14,568
I love you, Grandpa.

44
00:02:14,568 --> 00:02:20,364
You make me feel so proud to be part of our family.

45
00:02:20,364 --> 00:02:22,942
One day, you'll have your own family,

46
00:02:22,942 --> 00:02:27,480
and I'll be proud to be part of it.

47
00:02:27,480 --> 00:02:30,098
Now you understand my feelings, Susan.

48
00:02:30,098 --> 00:02:34,854
I'm Grandpa's daughter-in-law, but I feel like a Stewart.

49
00:02:34,854 --> 00:02:43,788
He's always made me feel like his own daughter.

50
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:44,208
Well,

51
00:02:44,208 --> 00:02:48,866
that's because you're so much like us--wonderful!

52
00:02:48,866 --> 00:02:49,744
Mom, got it.

53
00:02:49,744 --> 00:02:52,722
This will make a nice gift for Marilyn and Richard.

54
00:02:52,722 --> 00:02:55,227
They can keep a record of all of the important dates

55
00:02:55,227 --> 00:02:57,620
and information about Max's life here.

56
00:02:57,620 --> 00:02:58,678
Let's see.

57
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:02,227
Name: Max Stewart.

58
00:03:02,227 --> 00:03:04,634
Does he have a middle name?

59
00:03:04,634 --> 00:03:08,722
No, just Max. I like that.

60
00:03:08,722 --> 00:03:11,289
No middle name. No middle initial.

61
00:03:11,289 --> 00:03:15,047
Like me. I'm Malcolm Stewart.

62
00:03:15,047 --> 00:03:17,985
Just Malcolm Stewart.

63
00:03:17,985 --> 00:03:20,803
And Max has your initials, Grandpa:

64
00:03:20,803 --> 00:03:25,479
Uh, it must mean something.

65
00:03:25,479 --> 00:03:30,825
Weight: eight pounds six ounces.

66
00:03:30,825 --> 00:03:32,875
Eight-six. Big boy!

67
00:03:32,875 --> 00:03:35,746
All the Stewart men were big.

68
00:03:35,746 --> 00:03:39,291
Well, Robbie was eight pounds two ounces,

69
00:03:39,291 --> 00:03:42,097
and Richard was eight pounds three.

70
00:03:42,097 --> 00:03:43,347
And me?

71
00:03:43,347 --> 00:03:48,005
Eight pounds six.

72
00:03:48,005 --> 00:03:50,783
You were big, just like Max.

73
00:03:50,783 --> 00:03:53,481
Eight pounds six, just like me.

74
00:03:53,481 --> 00:03:56,484
That's nice. Length. Length?

75
00:03:56,484 --> 00:04:06,942
Richard says Max is twenty-one inches long.

76
00:04:06,942 --> 00:04:07,897
Twenty-one inches.

77
00:04:07,897 --> 00:04:08,097
Is that tall or average or what?

78
00:04:07,897 --> 00:04:10,149
Tall. All the Stewart men are tall.

79
00:04:10,149 --> 00:04:16,105
Well, Grandpa, you're about five-nine or five-ten.

80
00:04:16,105 --> 00:04:19,083
I wouldn't call that tall.

81
00:04:19,083 --> 00:04:22,727
I take after my mother's family.

82
00:04:22,727 --> 00:04:28,016
They were ... they were ... they were average.

83
00:04:28,016 --> 00:04:34,905
Mother: Marilyn. Father: Richard.

84
00:04:34,905 --> 00:04:41,068
And lots of pages for Richard's photos of Max.

85
00:04:41,068 --> 00:04:44,140
Speaking of mother and of father

86
00:04:44,140 --> 00:04:47,777
--and speaking of Max--I hear the car.

87
00:04:47,777 --> 00:04:55,485
They're here!

88
00:04:55,485 --> 00:04:58,963
Oh! Oh, quickly! Go, go, go!

89
00:04:58,963 --> 00:04:59,796
Let's see. Oh, welcome home.

90
00:04:59,796 --> 00:05:01,078
Oh, let her in.

91
00:05:01,078 --> 00:05:04,927
Wait with your pictures for a second.

92
00:05:04,927 --> 00:05:06,730
Come on, darlings.

93
00:05:06,730 --> 00:05:09,708
Sweetheart .... Sit down right here.

94
00:05:09,708 --> 00:05:12,348
Oh, he's so cute! Oh, Marilyn!

95
00:05:12,348 --> 00:05:14,686
Max looks just like Grandpa.

96
00:05:14,686 --> 00:05:15,664
A real Stewart.

97
00:05:15,664 --> 00:05:18,664
I'm so happy to be home with my family--and with Max.
